      "id": "seg:paragraph:overview:0009:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:overview:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The following example uses the [`UIViewController.ViewLoading`](uiviewcontroller/viewloading.md) wrapper to ensure that `dateLabel` [`UILabel`](uilabel.md) loads before referencing it in the `didSet` of the `date` property observer:",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example uses the [`UIViewController.ViewLoading`](uiviewcontroller/viewloading.md) wrapper to ensure that `dateLabel` [`UILabel`](uilabel.md) loads before referencing it in the `didSet` of the `date` property observer:",
      "sourceHash": "6bc40b4ff87562497c7e6642f05c392dbc2d0d2df1ecd9bdddbaad9ac68076f7",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Wrapping view controller properties this way eliminates crashes that can occur from implicitly defining properties as [`Optional`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Optional), and then referencing them before the view controller finishes loading.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nclass DateViewController: UIViewController {\n    @ViewLoading private var dateLabel: UILabel\n    \n    var date: Date? {\n        didSet {\n            let dateFormatter = DateFormatter()\n            dateFormatter.dateStyle = .full\n            let dateString = dateFormatter.string(from: self.date ?? Date())\n            // If the view controller's view hasn't loaded yet,\n            // accessing the dateLabel property here causes it to load.\n            self.dateLabel.text = dateString\n        }\n    }\n\n    override func viewDidLoad() {\n        super.viewDidLoad()\n        let label = UILabel(frame: self.view.bounds)\n        self.view.addSubview(label)\n        self.dateLabel = label\n    }\n}\n```",
      "documentTitle": "UIViewController.ViewLoading",
      "framework": "UIKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:overview:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "code:overview:0010",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nclass DateViewController: UIViewController {\n    @ViewLoading private var dateLabel: UILabel\n    \n    var date: Date? {\n        didSet {\n            let dateFormatter = DateFormatter()\n            dateFormatter.dateStyle = .full\n            let dateString = dateFormatter.string(from: self.date ?? Date())\n            // If the view controller's view hasn't loaded yet,\n            // accessing the dateLabel property here causes it to load.\n            self.dateLabel.text = dateString\n        }\n    }\n\n    override func viewDidLoad() {\n        super.viewDidLoad()\n        let label = UILabel(frame: self.view.bounds)\n        self.view.addSubview(label)\n        self.dateLabel = label\n    }\n}\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift class DateViewController: UIViewController { @ViewLoading private var dateLabel: UILabel var date: Date? { didSet { let dateFormatter = DateFormatter() dateFormatter.dateStyle = .full let dateString = dateFormatter.string(from: self.date ?? Date()) // If the view controller's view hasn't loaded yet, // accessing the dateLabel property here causes it to load. self.dateLabel.text = dateString } } override func viewDidLoad() { super.viewDidLoad() let label = UILabel(frame: self.view.bounds) self.view.addSubview(label) self.dateLabel = label } } ```",
      "sourceHash": "5f14c8c92346cf7aca8bcef01815f4bb3e170a7765219ae59040df6388f4c615",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "The following example uses the [`UIViewController.ViewLoading`](uiviewcontroller/viewloading.md) wrapper to ensure that `dateLabel` [`UILabel`](uilabel.md) loads before referencing it in the `didSet` of the `date` property observer:",
      "contextAfter": "After loading [`UILabel`](uilabel.md), the system can safely access and set the `date` property.",
      "documentTitle": "UIViewController.ViewLoading",
      "framework": "UIKit",
      "ko": "```swift\nclass DateViewController: UIViewController {\n    @ViewLoading private var dateLabel: UILabel\n    \n    var date: Date? {\n        didSet {\n            let dateFormatter = DateFormatter()\n            dateFormatter.dateStyle = .full\n            let dateString = dateFormatter.string(from: self.date ?? Date())\n            // If the view controller's view hasn't loaded yet,\n            // accessing the dateLabel property here causes it to load.\n            self.dateLabel.text = dateString\n        }\n    }\n\n    override func viewDidLoad() {\n        super.viewDidLoad()\n        let label = UILabel(frame: self.view.bounds)\n        self.view.addSubview(label)\n        self.dateLabel = label\n    }\n}\n```",
